out of the missed payment;","parentReference":"CONC 7.20.1R(2)(b)","conditions":[],"expertJudgement":[{"id":"adverse_consequences_scope","question":"Which consequences count as adverse (charges, credit reporting, enforcement, loss of facility)? The rule does not enumerate them."}]},{"reference":"CONC 7.20.1R(2)(b)(iii)","level":3,"label":"iii","kind":"content_element","legalEffect":"required_content_of_parent_limb","standaloneObligation":false,"text":"any adverse consequences for the borrower that the firm considers are likely to arise out of the missed payment; and","parentReference":"CONC 7.20.1R(2)(b)","conditions":[],"expertJudgement":[{"id":"firm_judgement","question":"The firm is asked to judge likely consequences. What evidence of that judgement is expected?"},{"id":"adverse_consequences_scope","question":"Which consequences count as adverse (charges, credit reporting, enforcement, loss of facility)? The rule does not enumerate them."}]},{"reference":"CONC 7.20.1R(2)(b)(iv)","level":3,"label":"iv","kind":"content_element","legalEffect":"required_content_of_parent_limb","standaloneObligation":false,"text":"(where relevant) any steps the borrower can take to mitigate those adverse consequences.","parentReference":"CONC 7.20.1R(2)(b)","conditions":["where relevant"],"expertJudgement":[{"id":"conditional_relevance","question":"When is a mitigation step \"relevant\"? The firm must decide per case; expert view on defensible criteria is needed."},{"id":"adverse_consequences_scope","question":"Which consequences count as adverse (charges, credit reporting, enforcement, loss of facility)? The rule does not enumerate them."}]},{"reference":"CONC 7.20.1R(3)","level":1,"label":"3","kind":"information_together_requirement","legalEffect":"binding_requirement","standaloneObligation":true,"text":"The information required under (2) must be provided together.","parentReference":null,"conditions":[],"expertJudgement":[]},{"reference":"CONC 7.20.1R(4)","level":1,"label":"4","kind":"definition_or_scope_qualification","legalEffect":"interpretation_or_scope","standaloneObligation":false,"text":"In this rule references to ‘payment’ refer to the repayment of capital but exclude payment of a charge for non-compliance with a regulated deferred payment credit agreement.","parentReference":null,"conditions":[],"expertJudgement":[]}],"standaloneObligationPaths":["CONC 7.20.1R(2)(a)","CONC 7.20.1R(2)(b)","CONC 7.20.1R(3)"],"applicabilityPaths":["CONC 7.20.1R(1)"],"definitionPaths":["CONC 7.20.1R(4)"],"expertJudgement":[{"id":"timing_as_soon_as_possible","question":"What period satisfies \"as soon as possible\"? The rule fixes no number of days; the FCA expectation on timing needs expert confirmation.","reference":"CONC 7.20.1R(2)"},{"id":"sufficiency_standard","question":"What level of detail is \"sufficient information for the borrower to understand\"? This is an outcome standard, not a content list.","reference":"CONC 7.20.1R(2)(b)"},{"id":"adverse_consequences_scope","question":"Which consequences count as adverse (charges, credit reporting, enforcement, loss of facility)? The rule does not enumerate them.","reference":"CONC 7.20.1R(2)(b)(ii)"},{"id":"firm_judgement","question":"The firm is asked to judge likely consequences. What evidence of that judgement is expected?","reference":"CONC 7.20.1R(2)(b)(iii)"},{"id":"adverse_consequences_scope","question":"Which consequences count as adverse (charges, credit reporting, enforcement, loss of facility)? The rule does not enumerate them.","reference":"CONC 7.20.1R(2)(b)(iii)"},{"id":"conditional_relevance","question":"When is a mitigation step \"relevant\"? The firm must decide per case; expert view on defensible criteria is needed.","reference":"CONC 7.20.1R(2)(b)(iv)"},{"id":"adverse_consequences_scope","question":"Which consequences count as adverse (charges, credit reporting, enforcement, loss of facility)? The rule does not enumerate them.","reference":"CONC 7.20.1R(2)(b)(iv)"}],"verbatim":"7.20.1 R (1) This rule applies where a borrower has failed to make a payment by the time it has fallen due under the terms of a regulated deferred payment credit agreement (‘a missed payment’). (2) As soon as possible after a missed payment has occurred the firm must: (a) notify the borrower: (i) that the missed payment has occurred; and (ii) about any sums which have become payable under the regulated deferred payment credit agreement but remain unpaid (including unpaid charges for non-compliance with the agreement); and (b) provide the borrower with sufficient information for the borrower to understand: (i) which regulated deferred payment credit agreement the missed payment relates to; (ii) any adverse consequences for the borrower arising out of the missed payment; (iii) any adverse consequences for the borrower that the firm considers are likely to arise out of the missed payment; and (iv) (where relevant) any steps the borrower can take to mitigate those adverse consequences. (3) The information required under (2) must be provided together. (4) In this rule references to ‘payment’ refer to the repayment of capital but exclude payment of a charge for non-compliance with a regulated deferred payment credit agreement."},"transitionalScan":{"provision":"7.20.1R","scannedTransitionalPages":[62,66,67,74,75,76,78,83,97,99,101],"provisionSpecificTransitionalFound":false,"mentions":[],"requiresExpertConfirmation":true,"note":"No transitional material in the instrument references this provision. This is a text search, not a legal conclusion on in-flight agreements or temporary-permission firms."},"commencementBackfill":{"reason":"FCA-EVAL-001 hardening: pilot materialised the obligation without a traced commencement date","source":"FCA PS26/1 instrument FCA 2026/2, Commencement paragraph clause H (PDF p.63), Annex F","computedBy":"legalRecordForProvision (deterministic, no AI)","computedFromFixture":"integrations/regulatory-sources/fixtures/fca-ps26-1-official.pdf","recordedA